Yes, yes, yes!

This has been said before, but it merits saying again. Most of the
artifacts are weak and dull. Looking at the list of non-quest-related
artifact weapons, we have:

Demonbane 	long sword
Excalibur 	long sword
Grayswandir 	silver saber
Snickersnee 	katana
Sunsword 	long sword
Cleaver 	battle axe
Giantslayer 	long sword
Magicbane 	athame
Mjollnir 	war hammer
Vorpal Blade 	long sword
Grimtooth 	orcish dagger
Orcrist  	elv broadsword
Sting 	elv dagger
Stormbringer 	runesword
Dragonbane 	broadsword
Fire Brand 	long sword
Frost Brand 	long sword
Ogresmasher 	war hammer
Trollsbane 	morning star
Werebane 	silver saber

Of 20 artifact weapons, 14 are some type of sword, and 7 are long
swords. There are three daggers, an axe, a hammer, and a morning star.
In a game where there are 25 potions alone that must be identified, 20
is not a large number. If people want less artifacts I'd say it has a
lot to do with the number of redundant artifacts in the game.

It seems to me someone made a patch a few months ago to even this out a
little. Certainly you could vary this up a bit. Dragonbane would make
an excellent lance or Polearm. Demonbane could be a silver mace.
Giantslayer a sling. What about others? More missile weapons?

AutoCrossbow - fires multiple quarrels a turn
Cupid's Arrows - chance to pacify or tame monster.
Magic Boomerang - Always returns the the wielder, even when it hits.
Chance to paralyze monsters. Retrieves objects. ( ;) )
Holy Hand Grenade - Powerful, one time use artifact, 3x3 area effect
that damages as an amplified fireball, makes craters in diggable floors
and destroys diggable walls.

Other ideas:
Staff of Magius - Permanent Light source. Provides MR/MC, Halves Power
cost for spells (i.e. something good for Wizards to try for that ISN'T
magicbane. Although really wizards are spoiled enough ;)
Diamond Scalpel - Ignores enemy AC. #engraves in 1 turn


Of course adding weapons makes the game potentially easier (assuming
you have them and not the enemy). But even so, I think it would be an
improvement to increase artifact diversity.



